WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.340
In 1980, an Oxford legal philosopher
published a book that rebuilt an old theory.

2
00:00:06.390 --> 00:00:10.430
John Finnis set out to
restate Aquinas' natural law,

3
00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:12.610
without first proving God.

4
00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:18.110
He named 7 basic goods, from life
and knowledge to friendship and play.

5
00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:22.150
Each one, he argued, is worth
having for its own sake.

6
00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:26.550
So are some human goods so basic
that you may never act against one,

7
00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:28.800
even to get a better result?

8
00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:33.550
In this mission, you'll meet his 9
requirements for pursuing the goods well.

9
00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:36.530
Then you'll test his theory
against proportionalism,

10
00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:39.210
on immigration and capital punishment.

11
00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:44.430
Your mission: weigh up whether some
goods are too basic ever to act against.
